I'll add to the other advice that a common error occurs if patch is 
expecting one sort of line ending (<cr><lf>) and the .diff has another 
(<lf>). In that case you need to change them over. I use vim (:set 
ff=dos or :set ff=unix) but there are other utilities (dos2unix and 
unix2dos I believe). I've no experience with Mac-style <cr> endings.

If you don't get errors, you don't need to worry about this.


